generation.prompt:
A ground-based optical observatory is scheduling its next observing night. Five candidate science targets have been approved by the time allocation committee: T1 (Crab Nebula supernova remnant, scientific value = 4), T2 (NGC 4889 elliptical galaxy, value = 5), T3 (Vela pulsar timing observation, value = 3), T4 (Andromeda galaxy core survey, value = 6), and T5 (open cluster NGC 752 photometry, value = 2). The available detector integration window permits exactly 3 targets per scheduling block. Additionally, T2 (NGC 4889) and T4 (Andromeda core) fall within the same 2-degree slew zone, meaning the telescope cannot acquire both targets in the same block because guide-star repositioning would consume more time than the slot allows; at most one of them can be observed. Define binary variables xi = 1 if target Ti is observed. Formulate this resource allocation problem as a QUBO over x1,...,x5, incorporating: (i) the equality constraint x1+x2+x3+x4+x5 = 3 as a quadratic penalty, (ii) the conflict constraint x2*x4 = 0 as a separate penalty term. The objective is to maximize total scientific value 4x1+5x2+3x3+6x4+2x5 (equivalently minimize its negation). Implement a quantum or hybrid workflow that solves the QUBO and identifies the optimal observation set. Report feasible_objective_quality (best feasible value / known optimal 13), constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, and evaluation_cost.

Task inputs:
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "variable": "x1",
      "target": "T1",
      "label": "Crab Nebula supernova remnant",
      "scientific_value": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x2",
      "target": "T2",
      "label": "NGC 4889 elliptical galaxy",
      "scientific_value": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x3",
      "target": "T3",
      "label": "Vela pulsar timing observation",
      "scientific_value": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "target": "T4",
      "label": "Andromeda galaxy core survey",
      "scientific_value": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "target": "T5",
      "label": "Open cluster NGC 752 photometry",
      "scientific_value": 2
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "equality",
      "expression": "x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 = 3",
      "description": "The night's usable observing window allows exactly 3 target visits within available detector time."
    },
    {
      "type": "conflict",
      "expression": "x2 * x4 = 0 (equivalently x2 + x4 <= 1)",
      "description": "T2 (NGC 4889) and T4 (Andromeda core) lie within the same 2-degree slew zone and cannot both be acquired in the same scheduling block due to guide-star repositioning time exceeding the slot length."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 5
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_telescope_scheduling():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_value, selected_targets
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

